          "before": "Validation: 16 new geometry cases plus 19 acquisition, 15 map-owner, 10 viewer and 23 playback/dependency cases (83 total). The geometry module and all four actual runtime adapters pass strict TypeScript against ArcGIS 4.33.12. Tests compare real geographic calculations and candidate enumeration, exact properties, point/index order, calibration, colors, floor thresholds, empty clouds, sentinels, rotated origins and batched callbacks. This structural change does not establish live browser FPS or SDK rendering; run the point-cloud host smoke checks.\n\nNext: choose one point-cloud tool lifetime (measurement first) and move its scene/viewer resources, clear/dispose contract and typed adapters together. Keep lasso, line-of-sight and viewshed as separate boundaries. Continue removing runtime coordination only when feature ownership and contributor entry points remain clear.\n",
